From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruiyangke <me@ry.ke>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] gpui: Pin Newport's GPUI snapshot

Pin the six gpui-pre 0.3.10 crates to ruiyangke/gpui-kit@5814f246
(branch newport/gpui-pre-v0.3.10). That branch is gpui-pre 0.3.10 (Zed
08cbb88) as GPUI Kit's generator stages it, plus Newport's GPUI patch
series in gpui/ on newport/patches.

The series adds an optional physical key and native layout metadata (original
key text, raw modifiers, lock states) to KeyDownEvent and KeyUpEvent, and
Window::numlock(). Newport's terminal needs them to encode keys the way a
terminal expects; GPUI's shortcut-oriented Keystroke drops them. Synthetic
events leave the fields empty, so shortcut dispatch is unchanged. Kit's event
constructors initialize the new fields; the gpui-fast backend is untouched.
The series also adds the Windows window, text input and file-drop hooks that
Newport's remote windows use; other platforms are unchanged.

Remove when GPUI exposes physical keys and layout metadata on key events and
the Windows hooks are upstream.
